## 1. The Big Idea

_One sentence: **Tracking hair is reading a 12-month chart, not glancing in a mirror — you lock a baseline, ride the expected Month-3 dip without flinching, take your first honest reading at Month 6, attribute each KPI's movement to the exact compound that owns it, and that reading routes you down one of four labeled branches.** The poster must make the reader feel, instantly, that the **interval is the discipline** (6 months is signal, 3 is noise; the dip is supposed to happen) and that the **chart is a decision instrument** (every line that moves names a knob you can turn) — replacing the anxious daily-shower-drain panic with a calm, gated, once-every-six-months verdict._

## 2. Visual Metaphor & Structure — the hero object

**A longitudinal trichoscopy chart-recorder: three KPI traces drawn left-to-right across a 12-month time axis, gated by hard vertical "audit lines" at Day 1, Month 6 and Month 12, with the Month-3 dread-shed rendered as an expected dip you ride through — and a four-branch decision fork peeling off the Month-6 gate.** This is the anchor; nothing replaces it. It reads as the chart clipped above a patient's bed: a medical strip-recorder, drafted with architectural restraint.

Read left to right (this matters — the eye must travel time's one-way arrow, the spine of the argument):

- **The TIME AXIS (the horizontal spine).** A single ruled baseline running the full width, ticked and labeled `DAY 1` · `MONTH 3` · `MONTH 6` · `MONTH 12`, with the spacing deliberately *non-linear and honest* — Day-1→M3→M6→M12 — and a small caption under it: `3 mo = noise · 6 mo = signal.` A faint `re-anchor every 12 mo ↻` loop-tick sits past Month 12.

- **The THREE KPI TRACES (the hero lines).** Three labeled traces run across the axis, each in its own lane, each tagged with its target band (the same numbers as 1.1's spec sheet, for continuity): `T:V RATIO ▸ >85% terminal`, `DENSITY ▸ 180–250 /cm²`, `SHAFT Ø ▸ 60–80 μm`. They start at a recorded **baseline node** at Day 1 (a small bracketed `[BASELINE LOCKED]` stamp) and travel rightward. Crucially, **each trace carries a small color-keyed "driver tag" pinned to it** — the attribution map made literal *on the line itself*: the T:V trace tagged `← RU58841 · α-E2`, the density trace tagged `← minoxidil · tretinoin`, the shaft trace tagged `← RU58841 · MK-677 · GHK-Cu`. (See §legend; this is the load-bearing concept and it lives *on the chart*, not in a footnote.)

- **The MONTH-3 DREAD-SHED DIP (the behavioral trap, coded as expected).** At the Month-3 tick, all three traces **dip together** into a shaded trough labeled `THE DREAD SHED — EXPECTED`, with the instruction stamp `HOLD. do not alter the protocol.` and a tiny mechanism gloss `weak telogen hairs pushed out → thicker terminal shafts incoming.` This dip is rendered in the **warm living register, NOT alarm red** — this is the single most important color decision in the poster: panicking here is the failure, so the dip must *not* look like danger. A thin ghost arrow shows the traces climbing back out of the trough after the dip. (Optional grace note: a faint "if you quit here" branch that dead-ends into a greyed-out `−9 months forfeited` stub — the cost of flinching.)

- **═══ THE MONTH-6 AUDIT GATE ═══** a hard **vertical rule** at Month 6 — the highest-contrast object on the time axis, the functional twin of 1.1's condemnation line but re-purposed as a **decision gate** rather than a point of no return. Caption above it: `FIRST TRUE AUDIT · compare to Day 1, same zone.` This is where the chart stops being a recording and becomes a fork.

- **THE FOUR-BRANCH DECISION FORK (peeling off the Month-6 gate, the lower-right payload).** Out of the gate, four labeled tracks diverge — each a compact `SYMPTOM → DIAGNOSIS → ACTION` card, color-keyed to *which trace misbehaved*:
  - **B1 · PARTIAL RESPONSE** — `T:V ↑ · density flat` → *vasodilator gap* → `audit minoxidil dose + coverage · confirm tretinoin layering`. (keyed to the density trace's driver)
  - **B2 · WAKE WITHOUT THICKENING** — `density ↑ · shaft flat` → *thickening gap* → `add GHK-Cu · cycle MK-677 8 wk · check RU vehicle`. (keyed to the shaft trace's driver)
  - **B3 · NO RESPONSE** — `all three flat` → *adherence / absorption / fibrosis* → `track every dose 4 wk · switch vehicle · T3 scan → if fibrosis >50%, transplant`. This branch carries the **only alarm red on the poster** (the fibrosis verdict — direct callback to 1.1's condemnation line; the chart can route you back to "this is now a surgery problem").
  - **B4 · MASS SHED** — `sudden spike, off-schedule` → *telogen effluvium* → `if Month 3: do nothing · if it tracks rapid fat loss: slow retatrutide to <1% bw/wk`.

- **THE MONTH-12 PEAK GATE (the verdict, far right).** A second vertical rule at Month 12, captioned `PEAK EVALUATION · the real delta is M12 vs DAY 1.` A small terminal stamp: `still slick & bare here = fibrosed → transplant` (the chart's only other touch of red — the article's hard landing). Past it, the `re-anchor ↻` tick restarts the loop.

**The tier ladder mapped ONTO the time axis (not a separate box).** The three measurement tiers from 1.1 are placed as *annotations on the gates*, so they teach *when* each tier is used: `DAY 1 → T3 (gold baseline)` · `MONTH 6 → T2 (Hair Doc, RM50, scan-only — demand the images, decline the package)` · `MONTH 12 → T3 (definitive)`. This is the article's exact split-tier strategy rendered as labels on the timeline rather than an orphaned ladder.

**The two-register surface (the locked device, reused).** Everything that is **observed tissue / biological state** — the traces, the dip, the follicle behavior — sits in the **warm living register** (terracotta). Everything that is **instrument / measurement / decision scaffolding** — the axis, the gates, the KPI bands, the tier labels, the fork cards' frames — sits in the **cool slate-blue measurement register**. Alarm red is rationed to exactly two marks: the **B3 fibrosis verdict** and the **M12 "still bare = fibrosed"** stamp — the two places the chart says *"chemistry is out of moves."* The surface itself teaches *biology-vs-instrument* and *recoverable-vs-permanent* before a word is read.

Why this metaphor fits and nothing else does: the article's literal structure is *a timed cadence* (axis with named gates), *an expected mid-course dip* (the trough), *an attribution key* (driver tags on the traces), and *a four-way decision* (the fork). A longitudinal chart-recorder with gated audit lines and a fork is the only object that holds all four at once — it is directional in time, it has named checkpoints, its lines *carry their own causes*, and it forks. A static three-state survey (that was 1.1's job, and repeating it would collapse the *what* and the *how* into one drawing) can't show *cadence* or *the dip*. A generic "12-month before/after" grid of head photos teaches nothing, hides the attribution, and re-introduces exactly the mirror-glancing panic the article exists to replace.

## 3. Layout Description

**Landscape is primary (~4:3 / 16:9)** — the hero is a horizontal time axis and needs left-to-right room for four gates plus the fork. (A portrait blog-hero variant works by stacking the decision fork *beneath* the chart instead of to its lower-right.)

- **Top band (~12%):** the headline (see §4), small against the bone paper, kerned wide, thin drafting border beneath, and a slug `Part 1 (The Diagnostic) · the How · Hair · the Attractive pillar`. A faint `TIME →` arrow primes the reading direction.
- **Center-left & center (~55%) — the hero chart:** the 12-month time axis with the three KPI traces, the Month-3 dread-shed trough (warm, `HOLD`), and the two hard vertical gates at Month 6 and Month 12. Driver tags pinned to each trace. Tier labels annotate the gates. This is the visual and conceptual mass of the poster.
- **Lower-right (~22%) — the four-branch decision fork:** the four `SYMPTOM → DIAGNOSIS → ACTION` cards peeling off the Month-6 gate, each keyed by color to the trace that misbehaved, B3 carrying the lone red fibrosis verdict. Reads as the chart's "what now" annex.
- **Right rail OR lower-left inset (~11%) — the attribution legend (the load-bearing key):** a compact 3-row key restating the driver tags as a clean table — `T:V ▸ RU58841 · α-E2` / `DENSITY ▸ minoxidil · tretinoin` / `SHAFT Ø ▸ RU58841 · MK-677 · GHK-Cu` — with the one-line rule `a line that moves names the knob that moved it.` Small enough to be a reference, prominent enough that the eye lands on it right after the traces.
- **Bottom band (~10%):** the thesis lockup (see §4) plus a **cadence micro-strip** restating the spine as four chips: `DAY 1 lock · M3 hold · M6 audit · M12 verdict`.

Reading path is deliberate and matches the argument: **enter top-left at the headline → drop to the Day-1 baseline node → travel right along the traces → hit the Month-3 trough and feel it's *expected*, not alarming → arrive at the Month-6 gate → fork down into the four branches → read the attribution legend to understand *why* each branch exists → continue to the Month-12 verdict → exit on the cadence strip.**

